Surface nature:  Pure PRESENTATIONAL primitive composing the shared <Tooltip>. The web source resolves one
                 string from its props (`resolved = i18nKey ? t(i18nKey,{defaultValue}) : text ?? ''`),
                 returns null when empty (`if (!resolved) return null`), and renders a focusable "?" button
                 that reveals an explanatory body (+ an optional "Learn more" link) on hover / focus / tap.
                 There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise — so it has NO loading / error / stale /
                 offline branch (nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect). Inventing such chrome would
                 fabricate states the source does not have, so this surface reproduces only the source's REAL
                 branches — the same faithful-parity stance as the sibling primitives ContextMenu (0206) and
                 DataTableColumnMenu (0210). The REAL branches, all reproduced:
                   • hidden        — no resolved content (web `return null`) -> native EmptyView; no telemetry.
                   • collapsed     — content present, tooltip closed -> only the trigger glyph renders.
                   • revealed      — tooltip open -> the body copy.
                   • revealed+link — body + the external "Learn more" link (valid URL -> Link; malformed URL
                                     -> non-interactive labelled fallback, never a crash).
                   • size variants xs/sm/md (web SIZE_CLASS 12/14/16pt); placement top/bottom/leading/trailing
                     (web top/bottom/left/right); the custom-glyph escape hatch (web `children`).
                 Browser facilities map to native peers: the Tooltip hover/focus reveal -> tap toggles a
                 `.popover` (the HIG "?" help-button idiom; dismiss on tap-outside/Escape for free) PLUS the
                 macOS hover system tooltip via `.help` PLUS the VoiceOver hint, so the copy is reachable by
                 pointer, tap, and assistive tech alike; web `placement` -> `.popover(arrowEdge:)` with
                 `.presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)` (stays a popover on compact iPhone width, not a
                 sheet); web `<a target="_blank">` -> SwiftUI `Link`; lucide `<HelpCircle>` -> SF Symbol
                 `questionmark.circle` scaled with Dynamic Type via `@ScaledMetric`.

Data sources reproduced (from web source):
  • useTranslation                 -> HelpTooltipStrings facade (P1/S10), table "HelpTooltip" + the caller's
                                      own body key resolved through the injected HelpTooltipResolve.
  • props (text/i18nKey/learnMore/  -> HelpTooltipController (@Observable @MainActor state-holder, P1/S8): it
    placement/size/ariaLabel)          resolves HelpTooltipContent once via the pure HelpTooltipProjector,
                                       exposes the derived accessible name + learn-more label, owns the reveal
                                       state, and emits the once-only view.opened (P1/S11).
  • content resolution rule         -> HelpTooltipProjector (Foundation-only, unit-tested): the verbatim port
                                       of `resolved = i18nKey ? t(...) : text ?? ''; if (!resolved) return null`.

